top stride_select

// A field selected at a stride that is not a power of two, `r[i*13 +:
// 13]`, as NewAE's clock-glitch module picks one of 32 glitch lengths out
// of a 416-bit register. As a shifter by the product it was a barrel
// shifter over every amount up to the base's width; `cellify` makes it a
// multiplexer on the bits of `i` instead, with a constant slice per value
// of `i`. Every value of `i` selects inside `r` here: past the end the
// unsynthesised select reads `x`, which the equivalence checker takes as
// free, so a golden that went there could only be `Different`.
// `cellify`'s own tests have the slices past the end and the product
// that wraps.
module stride_select
  net %r u52 wire
  net %i u2 wire
  net %y u13 wire
  port r in %r
  port i in %i
  port y out %y
  assign %y = %r[mul(resize(%i, u6), 6'd13) +: 13]
end
